description:
Variables store data. That's it. You create a variable with the syntax
```c
<type> <name> = <value>;
// or
<type> <name>;
// e.g.
int x = 12345;
char z;
```
You can re-assign to a variable/assign to a variable with `=`. So with our declared-but-not-initialized var `z`, we could do `z = 'h'`.
---
## Assignment:
We should store commonly used program data in variables. Create 2 variables, os_name, and revision, and assign os_name as `"BINDOS"`, and revision to `12`.

starterCode:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    // create your vars here.
    // don't touch below this line
    printf("%s %d", os_name, revision);
}
